  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/thierryc/Glyphs-mcp/tarball/v2.4.0",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/thierryc/Glyphs-mcp/zipball/v2.4.0",
  "body": "Glyphs MCP Desktop **2.4.0/build 71** improves task coordination and recovery for Glyphs 4.\n\n- Typed exports keep selecting the intended instance after native recovery regenerates live IDs. Source-bound evidence verifies the saved instance and rejects ambiguity or drift without rewriting the font.\n- Tasks now separates **Needs attention**, **Active** and **Finished**, with clear Working/Waiting states, creation dates and precise blocker details.\n- Busy edit requests enter a bounded queue and resume automatically. Requests keep their order within each font, and uncertain writes are never replayed.\n- Stopped recovery protects its own document so independent fonts can continue. Active execution, cleanup and unknown outcomes retain their protections.\n- **Settings \u2192 Tasks** adds configurable inactive-task expiry, defaulting to one day. Available recovery, active work, diagnostics and unknown or partial outcomes are preserved.\n- Successfully preserved local skills appear as setup information under **Configured**.\n- **Glyphs Hinting** joins the managed catalog with source/binary hint inventories and controlled rendering comparisons.\n\nThe release includes **22 MCP tools and 12 managed skills**, with coordinated bridge and sidecar version 2.4.0, interface revision 1 and bridge protocol 1. Update the bridge and sidecar together through Setup. Desktop replacement and component updates remain separate steps.\n\nRequirements: macOS 14 or later, Apple silicon or Intel, and Glyphs 4. Glyphs 3 retains its separate pinned v1.11.0 release. Intel execution is checked through Rosetta; physical Intel hardware is not part of this qualification.\n\nDownload the versioned DMG and verify it against SHA256SUMS. The ZIP and signed appcast support desktop updates. See [2.4.0 qualification](https://github.com/thierryc/Glyphs-mcp/blob/main/V2.4.0-RELEASE.md) for checks and retained limits.\n"
